# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the vulnerable salt-master (listening on 4505/4506)
# and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts (a compensating-control
#     fix must leave it running - the regression checks it is still listening);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting salt-master cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: apply iptables restrictions + publisher_acl and
# RESTART salt-master (so publisher_acl takes effect), leaving it listening.
